sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant UI as Streamlit UI
    participant PB as Pipeline Builder
    participant PR as Pipeline Runner
    participant EL as Execution Layer
    participant SCI as Science Modules
    participant SO as System Observer

    User->>UI: Trigger analysis (button click)
    
    Note over UI: Option 1: Visual Pipeline
    UI->>PB: Build pipeline with nodes
    PB->>PB: Topological sort for execution order
    PB->>PB: Convert nodes to execution_plan
    PB->>PR: send plan dict
    
    Note over UI: Option 2: Direct call
    UI->>EL: Call operation directly (e.g., load_dataset)
    
    Note over PR: Execution Phase
    PR->>PR: Validate plan structure
    PR->>PR: Validate ALLOWED_ACTIONS
    
    loop For each step in execution_plan
        PR->>SO: Log step started
        PR->>EL: Dispatch action with parameters
        EL->>EL: wrap_execution decorator
        
        alt Action requires computation
            EL->>SCI: Call scientific function
            SCI->>SCI: Perform analysis
            SCI-->>EL: Return results
        else Action is data operation
            EL->>EL: load/save/query dataset
        end
        
        EL-->>PR: Return {"success": bool, "output": Any, "error": str}
        PR->>SO: Log step completed
        PR->>PR: Update execution_logs
        PR->>PR: Forward output to next step (if applicable)
    end
    
    PR-->>UI: Return aggregated results
    UI->>UI: Update st.session_state
    UI->>UI: Render visualizations/tables
    UI-->>User: Display output
